1
00:00:00,260 --> 00:00:02,900
Mix-up number four: little spends don't

2
00:00:02,960 --> 00:00:03,300
matter.

3
00:00:03,760 --> 00:00:05,600
Now, I'm not telling you to stop buying

4
00:00:05,720 --> 00:00:06,120
snacks.

5
00:00:06,580 --> 00:00:08,440
One snack won't decide your future.

6
00:00:08,840 --> 00:00:11,120
Big things, like rent and debt, matter

7
00:00:11,180 --> 00:00:11,660
much more.

8
00:00:12,100 --> 00:00:13,820
But little spends show you what you

9
00:00:13,900 --> 00:00:14,840
really care about.

10
00:00:15,280 --> 00:00:18,000
Let's say you spend $20 a week on snacks

11
00:00:18,060 --> 00:00:19,620
you don't even enjoy that much.

12
00:00:20,080 --> 00:00:21,520
That's $80 a month.

13
00:00:21,880 --> 00:00:24,980
And over a whole year, that's $1,040.

14
00:00:25,420 --> 00:00:27,780
That could be a new bike, a family day

15
00:00:27,880 --> 00:00:30,020
out, or a big start on your savings.

16
00:00:30,480 --> 00:00:32,520
If the snacks make you happy, great,

17
00:00:32,820 --> 00:00:33,280
keep them.

18
00:00:33,640 --> 00:00:36,460
If not, you just found $1,040 for

19
00:00:36,560 --> 00:00:37,560
something you want more.

20
00:00:37,980 --> 00:00:40,220
Mix-up number five: once I make a

21
00:00:40,280 --> 00:00:41,520
budget, I'm done.

22
00:00:41,960 --> 00:00:43,620
A budget isn't a statue.

23
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:45,160
It's more like a garden.

24
00:00:45,540 --> 00:00:47,840
You check on it, pull a few weeds, and

25
00:00:47,920 --> 00:00:49,780
move things around when things change.

26
00:00:50,140 --> 00:00:51,020
Here's an example.

27
00:00:51,440 --> 00:00:52,960
Your friend's birthday is in three

28
00:00:53,060 --> 00:00:54,980
weeks, and you want to buy a $15

29
00:00:55,420 --> 00:00:55,840
present.

30
00:00:56,220 --> 00:00:58,180
If you wait until the day, you'll need

31
00:00:58,180 --> 00:00:59,840
$15 all at once.

32
00:01:00,260 --> 00:01:00,560
Ouch.

33
00:01:00,920 --> 00:01:03,320
But if you put away $5 a week for three

34
00:01:03,420 --> 00:01:05,260
weeks, the money is ready when the

35
00:01:05,320 --> 00:01:06,120
birthday comes.

36
00:01:06,520 --> 00:01:08,140
That's what checking your budget does.

37
00:01:08,520 --> 00:01:09,980
It helps you see what's coming.

38
00:01:10,380 --> 00:01:11,640
So look at it once a month.

39
00:01:11,960 --> 00:01:12,560
Ten minutes.

40
00:01:12,960 --> 00:01:13,500
What worked?

41
00:01:13,780 --> 00:01:14,340
What didn't?

42
00:01:14,660 --> 00:01:15,600
What's coming next?

43
00:01:16,020 --> 00:01:18,640
Mix-up number six: I messed up, so

44
00:01:18,700 --> 00:01:20,100
budgeting doesn't work for me.

45
00:01:20,460 --> 00:01:21,280
You will go over.

46
00:01:21,720 --> 00:01:22,440
Everyone does.

47
00:01:22,920 --> 00:01:25,280
Let's say you planned $30 for fun this

48
00:01:25,360 --> 00:01:27,100
month, and you spent $35.

49
00:01:27,940 --> 00:01:29,160
You went over by $5.

50
00:01:29,960 --> 00:01:31,120
That's not a disaster.

51
00:01:31,480 --> 00:01:34,360
Next month, you just plan $25 for fun,

52
00:01:34,740 --> 00:01:35,840
and you're back to even.

53
00:01:36,240 --> 00:01:37,900
It's like learning to ride a bike.

54
00:01:38,260 --> 00:01:38,880
You wobble.

55
00:01:39,160 --> 00:01:39,860
You fall off.

56
00:01:40,200 --> 00:01:41,100
You get back on.

57
00:01:41,420 --> 00:01:43,440
Nobody says, well, bikes don't work for

58
00:01:43,500 --> 00:01:43,680
me.

59
00:01:44,040 --> 00:01:46,180
The only budget that truly fails is the

60
00:01:46,280 --> 00:01:47,360
one you stop using.

61
00:01:47,740 --> 00:01:49,300
So what does it all come down to?

62
00:01:49,660 --> 00:01:52,360
Take away all six mix-ups, and budgeting

63
00:01:52,420 --> 00:01:53,840
is really just three jars.

64
00:01:54,260 --> 00:01:55,860
I call it the three-jar plan.

65
00:01:56,260 --> 00:01:57,800
Jar number one: needs.

66
00:01:58,160 --> 00:01:59,300
Things you must pay for.

67
00:01:59,600 --> 00:02:02,480
Your home, food, bills, getting to work

68
00:02:02,520 --> 00:02:03,000
or school.

69
00:02:03,380 --> 00:02:04,280
These come first.

70
00:02:04,580 --> 00:02:06,000
Jar number two: wants.

71
00:02:06,360 --> 00:02:07,180
The fun stuff.

72
00:02:07,540 --> 00:02:10,360
Candy, games, toys, eating out.

73
00:02:10,720 --> 00:02:11,840
Yes, you're allowed these.

74
00:02:12,200 --> 00:02:13,720
They just get their own jar.

75
00:02:14,100 --> 00:02:16,040
Jar number three: future you.

76
00:02:16,520 --> 00:02:18,880
Savings, your emergency fund, paying off

77
00:02:18,940 --> 00:02:20,680
debt, and later, investing.

78
00:02:21,080 --> 00:02:22,680
This is money that looks after the

79
00:02:22,720 --> 00:02:23,920
person you'll be next year.

80
00:02:24,320 --> 00:02:27,020
A simple way to start is the 50, 30, 20

81
00:02:27,080 --> 00:02:27,260
rule.

82
00:02:27,580 --> 00:02:29,900
Half goes to needs, about a third to

83
00:02:29,960 --> 00:02:31,880
wants, and a fifth to future you.

84
00:02:32,260 --> 00:02:34,980
Let's try it with a $10 allowance: $5

85
00:02:35,380 --> 00:02:36,420
goes in the needs jar.

86
00:02:36,420 --> 00:02:38,740
$3 goes in the wants jar.

87
00:02:38,740 --> 00:02:41,060
$2 goes in the future-you jar.

88
00:02:41,480 --> 00:02:43,180
Now let's try it with a grown-up's

89
00:02:43,180 --> 00:02:46,280
$1,000: $500 for needs.

90
00:02:46,280 --> 00:02:48,220
$300 for wants.

91
00:02:48,220 --> 00:02:50,340
$200 for future you.

92
00:02:50,720 --> 00:02:52,060
But here's the honest part.

93
00:02:52,420 --> 00:02:54,620
For lots of grown-ups, rent alone takes

94
00:02:54,680 --> 00:02:55,340
more than half.

95
00:02:55,740 --> 00:02:58,660
Say rent is $600 out of that $1,000.

96
00:02:59,440 --> 00:03:00,080
That's okay.

97
00:03:00,500 --> 00:03:01,540
You change the jars.

98
00:03:01,860 --> 00:03:06,060
Maybe $600 for needs, $250 for wants,

99
00:03:06,420 --> 00:03:08,900
and $150 for future you.

100
00:03:09,300 --> 00:03:11,660
That still adds up to $1,000.

101
00:03:12,040 --> 00:03:14,380
The numbers are a starting point, not a

102
00:03:14,440 --> 00:03:16,040
rule you get punished for breaking.

103
00:03:16,360 --> 00:03:18,940
The only must is this: future you always

104
00:03:18,980 --> 00:03:20,920
gets something, even if it's small.

105
00:03:21,340 --> 00:03:22,900
And here's the trick that makes it

106
00:03:22,960 --> 00:03:23,280
easier.

107
00:03:23,660 --> 00:03:24,860
Pay future you first.

108
00:03:25,220 --> 00:03:26,960
The moment money arrives, put the

109
00:03:27,000 --> 00:03:28,860
future-you money away before you can

110
00:03:28,980 --> 00:03:29,400
spend it.

111
00:03:29,760 --> 00:03:30,780
Watch how it grows.

112
00:03:31,120 --> 00:03:34,320
If a child saves $2 a week, that's $8 a

113
00:03:34,400 --> 00:03:34,680
month.

114
00:03:35,000 --> 00:03:37,740
In one year, that's $104.

115
00:03:38,140 --> 00:03:41,220
If a grown-up saves $200 a month, in one

116
00:03:41,280 --> 00:03:43,820
year, that's $2,400.

117
00:03:44,240 --> 00:03:44,840
Same idea.

118
00:03:45,180 --> 00:03:45,920
Different size.

119
00:03:46,380 --> 00:03:48,580
And it all starts by paying future you

120
00:03:48,660 --> 00:03:49,000
first.

121
00:03:49,400 --> 00:03:51,260
None of this makes you rich overnight.

122
00:03:51,720 --> 00:03:53,180
Budgeting isn't exciting.

123
00:03:53,520 --> 00:03:55,260
But it's the boring thing that makes the

124
00:03:55,300 --> 00:03:56,660
exciting things possible.

125
00:03:56,980 --> 00:03:58,560
The hard part isn't the math.

126
00:03:58,860 --> 00:04:01,100
It's checking in every month, even when

127
00:04:01,160 --> 00:04:02,080
you don't want to look.

128
00:04:02,440 --> 00:04:04,400
That's why I made the free Three-Jar

129
00:04:04,480 --> 00:04:04,920
Workshop.

130
00:04:05,240 --> 00:04:06,960
I'll show you how to set up your three

131
00:04:07,080 --> 00:04:09,400
jars step by step, even if you've never

132
00:04:09,460 --> 00:04:10,440
made a budget before.

133
00:04:10,860 --> 00:04:12,520
It's free, and the link is in the

134
00:04:12,560 --> 00:04:13,180
description.

135
00:04:13,520 --> 00:04:15,500
A budget isn't about saying no.

136
00:04:15,900 --> 00:04:17,720
It's about saying yes, on purpose.

137
00:04:18,100 --> 00:04:19,740
And now you know how the magic trick

138
00:04:19,820 --> 00:04:20,180
works.

139
00:04:20,580 --> 00:04:22,620
If you're ready, watch this video right

140
00:04:22,660 --> 00:04:22,880
here.

141
00:04:23,300 --> 00:04:24,620
It shows you what to do with your

142
00:04:24,740 --> 00:04:27,180
future-you jar once it starts to grow.

143
00:04:27,560 --> 00:04:28,520
See you in the next one.
